  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) Foundation: Conditional Gifts and Donations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) Foundation gifts and donations are considered conditional if the donor restricts its purpose or imposes a requirement that the gift be used: (1) To support a specific research study, project, or conference; (2) To support activities of a CDC employee identified by name or organizational title; (3) For specifically identified functions, such as observances, ceremonies, particular public information or health promotion campaigns, and community outreach activities; (4) For the purchase of specific items of equipment or other specific uses.</narrative>
  </description>
